review:
The pros:
- growing cities and developping production not by manually (and simply) placing buildings, but by supplying the cities and reaching demand;
- accompanning the evolution/modernization of vehicles and cities from 1850 to 2000;
- reaching positive income is only possible through prudent investments (made through loan, that generates monthly interest) - even in easy mode, money doesn’t come quickly;
- many of its management aspects for those who like the genre: vehicle proportion; supply and demand calculation; busses/trams frequency; vehicles maintanence/lifespan balance; route optimization; efficiency factors etc. 

The cons :
- the opacity of its AI: 
- “can’t connect the line”, “can’t find path” (precisely where?); 
- “construction not possible” (precisely in which tiles? Why?); 
- passenger lines usage: what causes the citizens not to leave their cars in order to use busses/trams? Uncovering this answer would be enjoyable if it was ever possible to really understand it clearly (check, for example, the lack of clear answers from the community in this thread https://steamcommunity.com/app/446800/discussions/0/143387886725592251/ compared to this guy, that has reached 80% passanger line usage with only unreasonable few bus stops: https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=828177211 ).
- Cargo transport by road seems unbalanced (for example, check the absurd number of vehicles of this "normal" profitable line: https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1401593643 ), there are always a bizarre number of vehicles in my road cargo lines;
-only insuffient 2x speed available;
- small soundtrack repertoires (everytime you start a game in a certain period, you'll listen to the same few songs for ingame decades);
- factories (etc.) sometimes will load too much cargo on one station and too little on another (there's no tool to prioritize stations loading; it’s suposed to automatically and perfectly work on demand, but of course it’s not always perfect and you have no direct means of intervening against this AI, as in https://steamcommunity.com/app/446800/discussions/0/224446340333618666/ );
- no “planning tool”: it’s impossible to plan (rail)roads or stations without having to actually build them (for example, by accident, sometimes I would place a cargo station instead of a passanger station and then I’d have to unrealistcly destroy it, to place the correct one); 


Conclusion
Some of these elements almost made me give up on TF and I had actually written a negative review while ago, before finally finding answers or learning to tolerate these negative/unbalanced elements that can’t be handled. Then I found that TF can be just: placing lines one after another for profit; or placing trains for the sake of trains - but only if you miss the cycle of 1. carefully expanding through decades of modernization and 2. (impossibly) managing to perfection the (ever more) complex network you’ve built through these decades.
